      "message": "Done. I just chose a position after footer starting index randomly and this one works.\n\nAnd surprisingly, not all positions trigger InvalidMetadata error. For example,\n\n- `RANDOM_FOOTER_POS`\u003d1, verification returns `Err(InvalidMetadata)`. \n- `RANDOM_FOOTER_POS`\u003d10, verification returns `Ok(())`. \n\nI thought the whole vbmeta data is signed, this somehow doesn\u0027t correspond to this understanding. wdyt? I\u0027ll investigate the code more closely later.",
